# Pattern fluency — 2026-11-12
#
# The owner asked to meditate on fluency of pattern navigation, extension and discovery; on use across computer science, linguistics, sociology, philosophy, anthropology, pure mathematics and musicology, with a lean toward library and information science; and on where a reader has a moment of discovery on spw.quest, factshift.center and in editors, into the nesting each feature makes possible. They asked for a caches and plan improvement pass after it.
# A reading with one count, operator inside operator, beside earlier counts on other grids. Nothing here is decided; the fields section is a set of leads unless it names a tree anchor.

#>journal_2026_11_12_pattern_fluency
#:cache #!observation
#:layer #!pragmatics

^["entry"]{
 date: "2026-11-12"
 kind: #observation
 base: "this repo at 9ef3d223 with the reading-drift and runtime-value slices uncommitted; the story consumer and the site consumer read in place; the two hosts read from the site consumer's working tree of the same day"
 method: "counted which operator sits inside which over five corpora with a scratch script on seed's parse columns, each surface read with its path; parsed one minimal form per ordered pair of twelve operators, in two spellings; read both hosts' source by excerpt through two survey agents and reread the lines cited here; read each hazard in the cut contract against the parser of the day with a form and a control"
 limits: "the hosts were read, not run, and the surveys list what they skipped (most of the canvas's nine modes, the quest's tests and data files); the fields section rests on works the caches tree does not source unless an anchor is named; the nesting count is operation inside operation only"
 corrects: "journal 2026-11-11-entrypoints-and-dreaming counted register stamps by grep and offered the question to interpretation-trials as if new: scripts/analyzers/spw-register-census.ts (988bd940) already reads every stamp against its bracket from tokens and found 12,151 of the site consumer's 12,387 restating on 2026-11-09, and wonder_trial_register already holds the question"
}

^["fluency"]{
 navigate: "following what a line already points at or sits in: a handle to its path, a citation to its anchor, a node to its parent, a plan to the files it touches; resolve, graph, tree, outline and the plan index doors serve it"
 extend: "changing one place and keeping the rest: a slot filled another way, a member added, a mark turned; three hosts build it (a pivot page, joint keys on a canvas, a night's one-slot turns) and line-kit slot_edits is the kernel they share"
 discover: "meeting the edge between what is written and what reads: a turn that lands on a line another page already holds, a pair of operators that reads and no corpus writes, a line whose reading moved while its text did not; rhymes, the count below and fingerprint --readings serve it"
 one_table: "all three walk the parse columns: beside and within for navigate, a hole in a shape for extend, a count over shapes for discover"
 fluent: "the three stop being separate: a reader who can follow a line can turn it, and a reader who turns lines sees where turns stop landing"
}

^["nesting"]{
 # Outer: the nearest enclosing operation's sigil. Inner: an operation's sigil. Twelve sigils, 144 ordered pairs.
 reads: "all 144 pairs read in the framed form a[o]{ b[i]{ x } }; in the named form aouter{ binner{ x } } the 23 pairs with @ read as another kind, since @name is a reference there"
 story_consumer: .{ surfaces: 100, operations: 4197, pairs_written: 76, pairs_for_half: 7, deepest: 4 }
 site_consumer: .{ surfaces: 492, operations: 44279, pairs_written: 52, pairs_for_half: 2, deepest: 5 }
 plans_here: .{ surfaces: 230, operations: 14532, pairs_written: 48, pairs_for_half: 2, deepest: 5 }
 canon_and_docs_here: .{ surfaces: 286, operations: 13993, pairs_written: 82, pairs_for_half: 4, deepest: 7 }
 caches_tree_here: .{ surfaces: 437, operations: 37384, pairs_written: 18, pairs_for_half: 2, deepest: 5 }
 together: "117 of 144 pairs are written somewhere, 13 in all five corpora, 46 in exactly one (the story consumer 25, canon and docs 15, the site 5, plans 1, the caches tree none), and 27 nowhere"
 pairs_for_half: "the fewest pairs that hold half of a corpus's nested operations: two in the site, the plans and the caches tree, seven in the story consumer"
 widest: "# sits inside all twelve and holds all twelve; ^ . ~ and ? each hold all twelve; $ holds four and = sits inside all twelve"
 reading: "what a feature adds is counted in pairs with the others, not in itself: a twelfth operator opens 23 ordered pairs with the eleven before it, and a host that gives a mark on a container its own behaviour multiplies those by how they look. The corpora written to a contract use few pairs heavily; the corpus written as a story world uses the most, from a fifth of the surfaces"
 limits: [
  "a spaced = reads as an operation, which is three quarters of the site's count (wonder_trial_spaced_equals)",
  "bindings, particles, annotations and path refs are on neither axis; the scratch output counts them against the enclosing operation and they are not reported here",
  "an unwritten pair is not a recommendation: a cell may be empty because nobody needs it (the grid gap finder's limit, tree anchor spw_lab_grid_gap)",
  "curiosity-mutation-ergonomics names a wider cell (sigil, boundary, occupancy, label, species); this is its sigil by sigil face only",
  "earlier counts sit on other grids: the grid gap finder's 36 of 52 operator by bound cells with no named step, and the coverage ranking of spw ls --seq in the operator-lattice skill, which scans operator and brace sequences and does not prove nesting"
 ]
}

^["fields"]{
 # What each field already practises that is one of the three motions. A line that names no tree anchor is a lead, not a sourced claim.
 library_science: [
  "facets: a faceted scheme builds a subject from parts joined by punctuation in a fixed citation order (tree anchor information_science_ko_colon); a brace pair that names its slot wherever it sits is the same move, and wonder_trial_slot_order asks what order is for once the mark names the part",
  "hospitality: how easily a scheme admits a subject it never listed (information_science_ko_hospitality); for a grammar the cost is the lines whose reading moves and the yield is the pairs and forms a change lets a writer use",
  "authority control: one preferred heading with its variants pointing at it (information_science_ko_thesauri) is the library form of one operator table with host aliases, the owner's open call words_travel",
  "work, expression, manifestation, item (information_science_ko_lrm): a surface as meant, its text in a dialect, a parser release, a consumer's pinned copy; the site consumer writes an expression = line on 262 surfaces, a rhyme of words and not a claim that it means that level",
  "trails: a named path through items that can be recalled and handed on (trail_index_memex); the site consumer's seeded walk asks for a trail a seed makes repeatable",
  "lead, the concordance: every occurrence of a unit printed with its line; fingerprint --readings --check prints file, line and text for each reading that moved, and a rhyme table is a concordance keyed by shape",
  "bibliographic coupling and co-citation (tree anchors spw_lab_coupling_map_kessler and spw_lab_coupling_map_small, where the coupling map builds both for claims and sources): the plan index's kin frame pairs plans that touch the same code with no declared edge, which is coupling, and its counterpart, two plans cited together by a third surface, is not computed",
  "lead, the reference interview: a need moves from felt to stated to formal to what a system can take; a wonder, a question, a question with a guess, a probe a night can run is that ladder, and inquiry-loop holds it"
 ]
 linguistics: [
  "the commutation test changes one element and asks whether the meaning changes; a one-slot turn is that test and a rhyme is its record, the forms that can stand in one hole",
  "a node's reading here is what it is, what it sits in and what it follows: its place in the chain, where a rhyme is its place in the column",
  "a readings snapshot is a gloss tier kept apart from the text (tree surface spw/contraptions/igt-aligner); drift is the gloss changing under text that did not"
 ]
 computer_science: [
  "one input through two builds, listing where they part, is differential testing; fingerprint --readings does it for a grammar",
  "the columns are a tree in preorder with subtree sizes, so each motion is a range scan and a second renderer can make it",
  "laws over generated lines (line-kit kit_laws) are the extend motion run by a machine before a person makes it"
 ]
 pure_mathematics: [
  "nesting is composition with arity; the count above is an incidence table of what composes with what in practice, 117 of 144",
  "lead: a table of which things occur together orders into a lattice of what is written with what; the appositions spw lattice lists are one such table"
 ]
 musicology: [
  "lead, paradigmatic analysis: a melody laid out so that units alike stand in a column and the piece reads across; a rhyme table is that layout for lines, and theme and variation is the one-slot turn as a form",
  "lead, reduction: a passage heard as nested levels from surface to frame; a body stepped through as written, by its parts and as particles, which the survey reports on the canvas, is the same listening",
  "the tree's perspectives index names musicians as a cluster with no perspective (spw_perspectives_index_missing)"
 ]
 sociology: [
  "lead, the boundary object: plastic enough for several groups to use and robust enough to stay one thing across them; a surface read by a parser, an editor, a canvas and a person is one where the readers agree, and reader agreement and host receipts measure where they part",
  "a scheme encodes the outlook of whoever maintains it (information_science_ko_bias); one operator table read by every host is also one outlook"
 ]
 anthropology: [
  "lead, entextualization: lifting a stretch of talk out of its setting so it can be carried and quoted; a kept line with who and when, a share fragment, a receipt, and a walk card that writes a visit as Spw are that act",
  "lead, bricolage: making with what is at hand; a host built from pivots and joints asks it of a visitor, and tinkering is its product name"
 ]
 philosophy: [
  "lead, noticing an aspect: the figure does not change and what is seen in it does; a line whose text hash holds while its reading moves is that event in a parser, and the moment a reader's own reading of a line changes is the discovery a host can stage",
  "two spellings with one reading (the separators the gate leaves out) and one spelling with two readings (a drifted line) are the two ways a mark and its meaning come apart"
 ]
}

^["discovery"]{
 # Where a reader meets something they did not expect. Host rows come from the surveys: read by excerpt, not run.
 what: "a discovery is a reading that changes while the text holds: the reader's, who sees what the line was all along, or the tool's, where a build reads it differently. A host can stage the first and owes a report of the second"
 command_line: "a count the writer did not know about their own corpus: the cache frame in 95 plan files, half of a corpus's nesting in two pairs, and the site consumer's own count of 75 pairs of lines one slot apart on different pages, 66 with no door"
 editors: "a hover that answers what is under the caret in one line, a lens that reads cited by nine files where the reader thought a file stood alone (editor-reading-hierarchy 2026-10-25), a rename that touches only marks of one kind (0ca23433)"
 editor_grammar: "each editor has a grammar of action of its own, and a unit of Spw offered once as an object of that grammar multiplies by every verb the editor has, where a unit offered as a command adds one; neovim-spw-surfaces says it as Spw that moves as Vim moves"
 spw_quest: "a line checked on each keystroke with a balloon that changes shape; a part held in the hand with what it would read before it is written; a pivot that shows the line a turn lands on and whether the shelf already holds it; two lines compared as the ground they share and the slot where they part; a walk written back to the visitor as Spw"
 factshift_center: "a line held on a canvas where each slot has a place and each separator a layout (a comma a ring, a semicolon a row, a dot a chain, ~> a rising path); a mark on a body's word gives that body alone a motion; joint keys where one tap shows the line a change would make and a second makes it; what does not read drawn as a faint region titled unread"
 across_hosts: "the same moves in different hands: prime, then actualize (wonder_trial_prime_actualize); the result shown before the commit on the surfaces surveyed, and none found that asks the visitor for a guess; one line carried between hosts by a share fragment"
 not_built: "no surface compares two parser builds, since the quest's parser index lists one release; the survey found no surface that asks the visitor for a guess before it answers, though the quest shows the form (a construct card with ~#expect, an example file with a prediction checked), the site consumer's own cache proposes a turn with a guess on record, and the caches tree's trails already write one"
}

^["offers"]{
 # None decided. Where one touches a plan it is logged in that plan's stream as an observation.
 guess_first: "one spelling for a guess written before a check, shared by trails, trials and wonders, so a host can ask for it and a night can score it (inquiry-loop)"
 both_columns: "a grammar receipt says what a change costs, the lines whose reading moved, and what it opens, the pairs and forms that read after and did not before (reading-drift, host-receipts)"
 separators_on_request: "a reading that keeps separators for hosts that draw them (reading-drift)"
 units_as_objects: "when a unit is lifted (a slot, a part, a joint, an anchor), offer it as an object every verb can take, a text object, a selector, a query hole, before it gets a command of its own (line-kit, neovim-spw-surfaces)"
 two_builds: "a readings diff between two parser cuts is the data for the two-release view the quest's plan holds (parser-releases)"
 turns_have_a_home: "the consumer's ask for turns that land fits line-kit, with rhymes as the index of where a turn lands (ask-exchange)"
 musicians: "the missing perspective has its notation here: a rhyme table read as a paradigmatic chart, a body's three drawings read as reduction"
}

^["passes"]{
 # The improvement pass the owner asked for, as run this day.
 hazards: "of the cut contract's thirteen hazards, ten hold as written; valence_keys no longer degrades a surface since f143ba31; a space does not cure prefix_path, a key or a body does; path_dialects did not reproduce in eight path forms and is kept as unconfirmed"
 tree_edits: "contract.spw, extend.spw and four surfaces that repeated the valence key hazard as a settled claim (spw/theory/valence-and-charge, spw/tokens-and-roles, spw/graph-idioms, spw/open-questions), each with a correction and a receipt"
 gates_before: "cut gate 437 files, 0 failing, 19 warnings; syntax validation 667 files passed; resolve 10,572 citations, all resolved"
 unindexed: "this entry and the two of 2026-11-11 (dreaming-in-spw, entrypoints-and-dreaming) are not in the journal index, which holds another session's uncommitted edit"
 plans: "stream entries dated this day in fifteen plans; seen lines on three trial cards; two findings parked in the lukewarm backlog; the index priority frame checked against the plans and not re-ranked; one cache status brought level with its card"
}
